Game: Venom
Players: 2

Cards:
  A deck called creatures, starting in the deck:
    | name   | health | copies |
    | Knight | 3      | 6      |
    | Archer | 2      | 6      |
    | Viper  | 1      | 4      |
  Cards can be poisoned.

Table:
  The deck is a pile in the center that no one can see.
  The discard pile is a pile in the center that everyone can see.
  Each player has a hand that only they can see.
  Each player has a camp row that everyone can see.

Setup:
  Shuffle the deck.
  Deal 4 cards from the deck to each hand.

Phase: playing
  Hint: Play a card to your camp, or draw one.
  Players take turns.
  A player may play a card from their hand to their camp.
    Then:
      Each poisoned card in their camp loses 1 health.
      If the card is a Viper, every card in the other player's camp is poisoned.
  A player may draw a card from the deck to their hand.
    Only if their hand is empty.
  When a card in a camp has 0 health:
    Move it to the discard pile.
  After a player plays or draws, the turn passes to the left.

End:
  The game ends when the deck and every hand are empty.
  The player with the most cards in their camp wins.

Example: a Viper poisons the other camp
  Given p0 holds a Viper
  And p1's camp has a Knight
  When p0 plays a Viper
  Then the Knight in p1's camp is poisoned

Example: a freshly poisoned card loses no health yet
  Given p0 holds a Viper
  And p1's camp has a Knight
  When p0 plays a Viper
  Then the Knight in p1's camp has 3 health

Example: poisoned cards lose health when their owner plays
  Given it is p1's turn
  And p1 holds an Archer
  And p1's camp has a Knight
  And the Knight in p1's camp is poisoned
  When p1 plays an Archer
  Then the Knight in p1's camp has 2 health

Example: a card at 0 health goes to the discard pile
  Given it is p1's turn
  And p1 holds an Archer
  And p1's camp has a Viper
  And the Viper in p1's camp is poisoned
  When p1 plays an Archer
  Then the discard pile has a Viper
  And p1's camp has an Archer

Example: an unpoisoned card keeps its health
  Given it is p1's turn
  And p1 holds an Archer
  And p1's camp has a Knight
  When p1 plays an Archer
  Then the Knight in p1's camp has 3 health

Example: you draw only with an empty hand
  Given p0 holds a Knight
  When p0 draws a card
  Then it is rejected because "their hand is empty"

Example: the most cards in a camp wins
  Given the deck is empty
  And p0 holds a Knight
  And p1's hand is empty
  And p0's camp has a Knight
  And p1's camp has an Archer
  When p0 plays a Knight
  Then p0 wins
